\fs32\b Getting Started\b0\fs20\par
\par
WinBMD2 is used to transcribe entries from images of the General Register Office indexes for submission to FreeBMD.\par
\par
\fs24\b Starting a transcription\b0\fs20\par
Use the File commands to start a new transcription or open an existing transcription file.\par
\par
When starting a new transcription, enter the batch information required to identify the index being transcribed. When opening an existing file, WinBMD2 reads the information stored in that file and restores the transcription for you.\par
\par
\fs24\b Displaying the scan\b0\fs20\par
The scan is displayed in the separate ScanView window. The transcription window and ScanView window can be resized and positioned independently, which is particularly useful when using more than one monitor.\par
\par
WinBMD2 can automatically locate and display the scan associated with the current transcription when sufficient source information is available.\par
\par
\fs24\b Transcribing entries\b0\fs20\par
Enter the information from the scan into the transcription grid. Use Tab or Enter to move through the fields and continue to the next entry.\par
\par
WinBMD2 provides validation, picklists and other entry aids to help reduce transcription errors. See the Transcribing and The Grid topics for more information.\par
\par
\fs24\b Verifying the transcription\b0\fs20\par
After entries have been transcribed, use the Verify commands to compare the transcription with the scan and confirm that each entry is correct.\par
\par
See the Verification topic for details of the verification process.\par
\par
\fs24\b Saving your work\b0\fs20\par
Your transcription can be saved and reopened later so that you do not have to complete a batch in one session.\par
\par
See the Files topic for information about opening, saving and managing transcription files.\par
\par
\fs24\b Uploading to FreeBMD\b0\fs20\par
When the transcription is complete and has passed the required checks, use the Upload commands to submit it to FreeBMD.\par
\par
See the Uploading topic for details of the checks performed before upload and the upload process itself.\par
\par
\fs24\b More help\b0\fs20\par
Select a topic from the list on the left for more detailed information about a particular part of WinBMD2.\par
\par
The Keyboard Shortcuts topic provides a quick reference to the keys used while transcribing.\par
